    "title": "Clean-endpoint Picard-kernel elementary-modification dichotomy",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "exact finite-pushforward and bundle classification",
    "statement": "The clean multiplication kernel is pi_*O_C(P_*), a length-one positive elementary modification of pi_*O_C=O+O(-rho)^(m-1). Hence it has exactly one of two splittings: O(1)+O(-rho)^(m-1), with two sections and C isomorphic to P^1, or O+O(1-rho)+O(-rho)^(m-2), with one section. Thus the bare injectivity/all-negative-splitting route is impossible and the clean frontier splits into these two branches.",
